title: 'Discovery: agent learning loop infrastructure already exists — unconnected'
summary: 'Deep codebase audit revealed that Paradigm already has all the pieces for a closed agent learning loop — lore with confidence/assessment/calibration, habits with practice events and graduation, session stats with tool usage tracking, notebooks for curated knowledge, and programmatic CLAUDE.md generation. The critical finding: none of these systems feed back into agent behavior. The observation layer is complete; the adaptation layer is missing entirely. This is the jumping-off point for a foundational discussion about how the framework should learn from its own usage.'
